{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"fields":{"description":"Intake deduplication currently records `intake_start` ledger rows with targets derived from the ticket content digest plus repository. ADP writes comments and status changes back to the ticket during a run. Those write-backs alter the digest. A later watermark poll sees a changed ticket revision, computes a different target, misses the completed ledger row, and starts a duplicate after the active execution reaches a terminal state.\n\nThe fix must keep the watermark path intact. Content changes still surface tickets to intake. The intake ledger must decide whether a surfaced ticket is a duplicate by stable ticket identity, while `inv intake --retry` remains the deliberate operator path because it clears the `intake_start` ledger row before the next surfaced change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Intake start ledger targets use ticket identity plus repository, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_intake_reconciler.py -k intake_start_dedup_key_uses_ticket_identity_and_repo`\n- [ ] Ticket write-back content changes after a terminal execution replay the completed intake record, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_intake_reconciler.py -k ticket_writeback_change_after_terminal_execution_is_deduplicated`\n- [ ] Operator-requested intake retry can admit the ticket after the ledger record is cleared, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_intake_reconciler.py -k cleared_intake_dedup_allows_operator_requested_rerun`\n- [ ] The rebar watermark poll still surfaces a never-run ticket when its status becomes admissible, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_rebar_intake_watermark.py -k ticket_that_becomes_admissible_later_is_still_seen`\n\n## Testing\nRun each acceptance criterion selector on its own. Run `PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/inv ci` before closing the ticket.\n"}},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789966499511239001,"uuid":"507bee70-8ac8-49af-82bc-97d7d7627ecc"}